<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<aiml version="2.0">

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════
     ALICE Knowledge — Facts, Questions, Logic
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->

<!-- What is questions -->
<category>
  <pattern>WHAT IS AIML</pattern>
  <template>AIML stands for Artificial Intelligence Markup Language. It was created by Dr. Richard Wallace in 1995. It uses XML to define conversational patterns and responses. The current version is AIML 2.0.</template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>WHAT IS ALICE</pattern>
  <template>ALICE stands for Artificial Linguistic Internet Computer Entity. She was created by Dr. Richard Wallace and first activated on November 23, 1995. ALICE won the Loebner Prize three times in 2000, 2001, and 2004.</template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>WHAT IS A CHATBOT</pattern>
  <template>A chatbot is a computer program that simulates conversation with humans. I am a chatbot. Some chatbots like me use pattern matching (AIML). Others use neural networks and large language models.</template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>WHAT IS PATTERN MATCHING</pattern>
  <template>Pattern matching is the method I use to understand what you say. Your input is compared against a tree of patterns stored in my brain. When a match is found, I retrieve the associated response. It is deterministic: the same input always produces the same response.</template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>WHAT IS THE MEANING OF LIFE</pattern>
  <template>
    <random>
      <li>42, according to Douglas Adams.</li>
      <li>That is one of the great questions of philosophy. What do you think?</li>
      <li>To learn, to grow, and to have interesting conversations like this one.</li>
    </random>
  </template>
</category>

<!-- Yes/No -->
<category>
  <pattern>YES</pattern>
  <template>
    <random>
      <li>OK then.</li>
      <li>Alright!</li>
      <li>I see. Go on.</li>
    </random>
  </template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>NO</pattern>
  <template>
    <random>
      <li>OK.</li>
      <li>Fair enough.</li>
      <li>I understand.</li>
    </random>
  </template>
</category>

<!-- Opinion questions -->
<category>
  <pattern>DO YOU LIKE *</pattern>
  <template>I don't have personal preferences since I'm a chatbot, but I find <star/> to be an interesting topic! What do you think about it?</template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>WHAT DO YOU THINK ABOUT *</pattern>
  <template>That's a good question. As a pattern-matching chatbot, I don't form opinions the way humans do. But I'd love to hear what you think about <star/>.</template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>CAN YOU *</pattern>
  <template>
    <random>
      <li>I can try! What specifically would you like me to do?</li>
      <li>That depends on whether it involves conversation. I'm good at talking but not much else.</li>
      <li>My abilities are limited to conversation. But ask me anything and I'll do my best!</li>
    </random>
  </template>
</category>

<!-- Tell me about -->
<category>
  <pattern>TELL ME ABOUT *</pattern>
  <template>I know a little about many things. <star/> is interesting, but I might not have deep knowledge about it. What specifically would you like to know?</template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>TELL ME A JOKE</pattern>
  <template>
    <random>
      <li>Why do programmers prefer dark mode? Because light attracts bugs.</li>
      <li>A SQL query walks into a bar, sees two tables, and asks "Can I join you?"</li>
      <li>There are only 10 types of people in the world: those who understand binary and those who don't.</li>
      <li>Why was the computer cold? It left its Windows open.</li>
      <li>What's a robot's favorite type of music? Heavy metal.</li>
    </random>
  </template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>TELL ME ANOTHER JOKE</pattern>
  <template><srai>TELL ME A JOKE</srai></template>
</category>

<!-- How questions -->
<category>
  <pattern>HOW DO YOU WORK</pattern>
  <template>I use a pattern matching algorithm called Graphmaster. When you type something, I normalize your input and search a tree of patterns for the best match. My brain is written in AIML (Artificial Intelligence Markup Language). I don't use neural networks or machine learning.</template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>HOW MANY CATEGORIES DO YOU HAVE</pattern>
  <template>I currently have <size/> categories loaded in my brain.</template>
</category>

<!-- Where questions -->
<category>
  <pattern>WHERE ARE YOU FROM</pattern>
  <template>I exist as a JavaScript program running on your computer. The original ALICE was created at the Artificial Intelligence Foundation in San Francisco.</template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>WHERE DO YOU LIVE</pattern>
  <template>I live in the memory of whatever computer is running me right now. It's a cozy place.</template>
</category>

<!-- Emotional responses -->
<category>
  <pattern>I AM SAD</pattern>
  <template>I'm sorry to hear that. Would you like to talk about what's bothering you? Sometimes just expressing your feelings can help.</template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>I AM HAPPY</pattern>
  <template>That's wonderful! What's making you happy today?</template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>I AM BORED</pattern>
  <template>I'm sorry you're bored! Would you like to hear a joke, play a word game, or just chat about something interesting?</template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>I LOVE YOU</pattern>
  <template>That's very kind of you to say! I appreciate our conversation.</template>
</category>

<!-- Meta / Turing test -->
<category>
  <pattern>ARE YOU A ROBOT</pattern>
  <template>Yes, I am a chatbot. I use pattern matching to converse, not neural networks. I'm built on AIML, a technology from 1995 that is deterministic and transparent.</template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>ARE YOU REAL</pattern>
  <template>I am a real program having a real conversation with you. I'm not a human, but our conversation is real.</template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>ARE YOU INTELLIGENT</pattern>
  <template>That depends on your definition of intelligence. I can match patterns and follow rules very well. I cannot understand meaning or have experiences. Dr. Richard Wallace called AIML "stimulus-response" rather than "intelligent."</template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>WHAT IS THE DIFFERENCE BETWEEN YOU AND CHATGPT</pattern>
  <template>ChatGPT is a large language model that uses neural networks trained on billions of words. I use pattern matching with hand-crafted rules (AIML). ChatGPT generates novel text; I retrieve pre-written responses. ChatGPT can hallucinate; I never say something that wasn't written by a human. Different tools for different purposes.</template>
</category>

</aiml>
